<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Horatii and Curiatii</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Horatii, Curiatii</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Horatii and Curiatii were two sets of triplet brothers who, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a>, fought a duel to decide the war between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and Alba Longa under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tullus-hostilius">Tullus Hostilius</a> in the mid-7th century BCE. Two Roman Horatii fell, but the survivor killed all three Albans, and Alba submitted to Rome. The story became a model of civic virtue, painted by Jacques-Louis <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> in 1784.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/horatii-and-curiatii.jpg" alt="Horatii and Curiatii" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anne-Louis Girodet / After Jacques-Louis David · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques-Louis_David_-_Oath_of_the_Horatii_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
